## One deviation, flagged

The line's steps alone do not satisfy its own verify. Without extra work the advisor in the arena exits `69` with `@spec-kit/system-skill-advisor dist is stale`, because `git clone` stamps every source with the checkout time while `cp -Rc` preserves the compiled build's older mtime, and the freshness guard's path-keyed cache record cannot survive a move to a new absolute path. I added one step after each copied `dist` tree: set its timestamps to the copy time, so the copied build (the same commit's build) looks newer than the checkout, as a build run there would. Evidence: before the step, `checkPackageFreshness` returned `status: "stale"` via the mtime branch; after it, `fresh` for both entries and the CLI returns a recommendation. The step touches only files inside the arena.

## Notes

- `cp -Rc` is BSD/macOS (`-c` = APFS clonefile), as the line names it. GNU `cp` has no `-c`, so this script is macOS-only by construction.
- Ignore status is asked of git per path (`check-ignore`), so a directory named `dist` that is tracked is left to the clone instead of copied over.
- Dotenv skip is at copy time, at every depth, not a copy-then-delete. `find` over the copied trees of the real arena returns no dotenv file.
- Build takes ~30 s (10 s clone + copy of ~2 GB of packs and 1.3 GB of tree).
